			<item>
				<title>Change default kernel</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/change-default-kernel/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 16:58:36 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/change-default-kernel/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;change-default-kernel&#34;&gt;Change default kernel&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#change-default-kernel&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote class=&#39;book-hint note&#39;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This guide is for systems using the default &lt;code&gt;systemd-boot&lt;/code&gt; UEFI boot manager in Endeavour OS.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;Your system can have multiple kernels (or versions) of Linux. The default kernel is usually the latest version, but can be adjusted to user preference.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, you need to identify and adjust the kernel &lt;code&gt;ids&lt;/code&gt; used in the &lt;code&gt;boot loader&lt;/code&gt; config file.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;find-kernel-id-with-bootctl&#34;&gt;Find kernel &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;bootctl&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#find-kernel-id-with-bootctl&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;book-steps&#34; &gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Change to the root user with &lt;code&gt;sudo -s&lt;/code&gt; and enter your password.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Downgrade with eos-shifttime</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/downgrade-to-specific-date/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 13 May 2026 14:09:31 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/downgrade-to-specific-date/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;downgrade-with-eos-shifttime&#34;&gt;Downgrade with &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#downgrade-with-eos-shifttime&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote class=&#39;book-hint warning&#39;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; does not revert AUR packages. The downgrade only applies to official Arch packages from the archive repositories.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; application can revert system packages to their state at a specified date.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;book-steps&#34; &gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Open a terminal window and run &lt;code&gt;eos-shifttime&lt;/code&gt; with root permissions.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Select the date to revert to on the GUI window, then click &lt;strong&gt;Revert&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;img src=&#34;https://redzhift.github.io/images/eos-shifttime.png&#34; alt=&#34;A GUI window for the eos-shifttime tool displaying a monthly calendar. The selected date is January 2, 2026.&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Install new theme in Typora</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/install-new-theme-in-typora/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 25 Jun 2026 10:37:17 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/user-config/install-new-theme-in-typora/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;install-new-theme-in-typora&#34;&gt;Install new theme in Typora&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#install-new-theme-in-typora&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;book-steps&#34; &gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typora&lt;/strong&gt; is a minimalist text editor that renders markdown and code in real-time. The software comes with several default themes that can be applied through the &lt;strong&gt;Themes&lt;/strong&gt; option menu.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;First, find which custom theme you&amp;rsquo;d like to install from the &lt;a href=&#34;https://theme.typora.io/&#34;&gt;Typora themes page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Download&lt;/strong&gt; the theme.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Typora&lt;/strong&gt; and navigate to the &lt;strong&gt;File &amp;gt; Preferences&lt;/strong&gt; menu. The keyboard shortcut is &lt;code&gt;Ctrl + comma&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://redzhift.github.io/images/typora-1.png&#34; alt=&#34;The Appearance tab in the Preferences options menu&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Update packages</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/update-packages/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 12 May 2026 14:09:31 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/update-packages/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;update-packages&#34;&gt;Update packages&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#update-packages&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There are 3 commands used to update &lt;strong&gt;Endeavour OS&lt;/strong&gt; systems:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;pacman - Syu&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;yay&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;eos-update&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote class=&#39;book-hint note&#39;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Some commands require prepending &lt;code&gt;sudo&lt;/code&gt; as they require &lt;code&gt;super user&lt;/code&gt; (or root) permissions to run.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;However, &lt;code&gt;yay&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;eos-update&lt;/code&gt; do not require &lt;code&gt;sudo&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;pacman--syu&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pacman -Syu&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#pacman--syu&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;pacman&lt;/code&gt; is the package manager used to install and update programs in Arch Linux.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To perform a full system update and refresh, run:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ sudo pacman -Syu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;details &gt;&lt;summary&gt;Example terminal output&lt;/summary&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;markdown-inner&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;user@computer ~&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; $ sudo pacman -Syu&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;sudo password &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; user&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;: *&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; :: Synchronizing package databases...&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; endeavouros       17.0 KiB   3.17 KiB/s 00:05 &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;--------------&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; 100%&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; core             117.4 KiB   23.3 KiB/s 00:05 &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;--------------&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; 100%&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; extra              8.0 MiB   &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1447&lt;/span&gt; KiB/s 00:06 &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;--------------&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; 100%&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; multilib         125.4 KiB    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;416&lt;/span&gt; KiB/s 00:00 &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;--------------&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; 100%&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; :: Starting full system upgrade...&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; resolving dependencies...&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; looking &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; conflicting packages... &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; Package &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;2&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;           Old Version  New Version  Net Change  Download Size&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; endeavouros/package-1    25.11-1   25.11.1-1     0.00 MiB    0.02 MiB&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; endeavouros/package-2    12.5.2-2  12.5.3-1      0.02 MiB    3.20 MiB &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; Total Download Size:   3.21 MiB &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; Total Installed Size:  9.42 MiB&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; Net Upgrade Size:      0.02 MiB&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;                                     &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# enter Y to confirm&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; :: Proceed with installation? &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;Y/n&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;       &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;# n to cancel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/details&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other &lt;code&gt;pacman&lt;/code&gt; options&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Re-rank mirrors</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/rerank-mirrors/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 18:00:22 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/rerank-mirrors/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;re-rank-mirrors&#34;&gt;Re-rank mirrors&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#re-rank-mirrors&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mirrors&lt;/strong&gt; are servers located around the world that store copies of software packages.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When upgrading packages, your EndeavourOS system utilizes multiple mirrors, which are noted in a &lt;code&gt;mirrorlist&lt;/code&gt;. Outdated mirrors can prevent &lt;code&gt;pacman&lt;/code&gt; from updating &lt;strong&gt;core packages&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;book-tabs&#34; &gt;&#xA;&lt;input type=&#34;radio&#34; class=&#34;toggle&#34; name=&#34;tabs-&amp;lt;nil&amp;gt;&#34; id=&#34;tabs-&amp;lt;nil&amp;gt;-0&#34; checked=&#34;checked&#34; /&gt;&lt;label for=&#34;tabs-&amp;lt;nil&amp;gt;-0&#34;&gt;Re-rank Arch mirrors&lt;/label&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;book-tabs-content markdown-inner&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Update the Arch &lt;code&gt;mirrorlist&lt;/code&gt; by running:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ reflector-simple&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;details &gt;&lt;summary&gt;reflector-simple GUI tool&lt;/summary&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;markdown-inner&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://redzhift.github.io/images/reflector-simple-1.png&#34; alt=&#34;reflector-simple graphical tool showing options such as mirror location and ranking priority.&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/details&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;book-steps&#34; &gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Adjust your preferences in the &lt;code&gt;reflector-simple&lt;/code&gt; GUI tool. You can choose the number of mirrors to store in your mirrorlist, the country of origin, and ranks based on speed or age.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>FAQs</title>
				<link>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/faqs/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 12 May 2026 14:09:31 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/faqs/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;faqs&#34;&gt;FAQs&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#faqs&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;why-do-i-get-errors-when-i-try-to-update&#34;&gt;Why do I get errors when I try to update?&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#why-do-i-get-errors-when-i-try-to-update&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Outdated package databases will cause errors when &lt;code&gt;pacman&lt;/code&gt; tries to retrieve the latest package files.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This can be prevented through regular &lt;a href=&#34;https://redzhift.github.io/docs/user-guides/system-maintenance/rerank-mirrors&#34;&gt;mirror maintenance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;details &gt;&lt;summary&gt;Error: failed to commit transaction (conflicting files)&lt;/summary&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;markdown-inner&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Error: failed to commit transaction (conflicting files)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Running a &lt;code&gt;sudo pacman -Syu&lt;/code&gt; update may fail and display the following errors:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; error: failed to commit transaction &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;conflicting files&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; &amp;lt;example&amp;gt;: /example exists in filesystem &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;owned by filesystem&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt; &amp;lt;example&amp;gt;: /lib/systemd/system/example.service exists in filesystem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;These issues can be resolved with manual intervention. Uninstall and remove the package from the system, then reinstall/update with these two commands:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
	</channel>
